The Silver Key is the single most convenient way, but having got it
means you got a convenience, rather than something actually useful, for
a Crowning gift. Which sucks a bit.

Otherwise, having a full set of normal keys is the most convenient IME.
In time, you end up with so many spares that they become a minor
annoyance -- almost too heavy in sum to just ignore, too tedious to
periodically stash away.

There are a *lot* of doors in ADOMland. You do *not* want to go through
extra keypresses for each one (the skill-based approach). Shame those
skills aren't auto-used here. :-{

Erm... I'm sure there's some lesson here about "random keys that don't
suck."

Actually, I don't mind the key system in ADOM, mainly because it's not
all-or-nothing, but a set of various tradeoffs (buy a key? wait for a
key? risk damage from a door trap? save time by not dropping my stuff
and risk item destruction? etc.), and that works out OK.

